100
00:04:55,382 --> 00:04:59,025
with a therapist in the community, either for mental health or substance use.

101
00:04:59,485 --> 00:05:06,430
There are two forms that they can access this service, and I'm going to walk you through all of it.

102
00:05:06,450 --> 00:05:08,011
I'm going to share my screen if that's all right.

103
00:05:11,013 --> 00:05:17,217
So the first thing is this is what we sent out to all of our families and our staff, along with a message.

104
00:05:17,257 --> 00:05:22,621
It was translated into our top three languages of Portuguese, Haitian, Creole, and Arabic.

105
00:05:23,698 --> 00:05:29,242
And families can either access the service themselves by going online.

106
00:05:29,262 --> 00:05:30,423
I'll show that to you next.

107
00:05:31,124 --> 00:05:38,250
Or they can connect with either an administrator, assistant principals, principals, or a counselor.

108
00:05:38,370 --> 00:05:42,373
All counseling staff have ability to do what I'm going to show you as a warm handoff.

109
00:05:44,235 --> 00:05:53,238
If people are searching on their own, they go to our Medford public school site or Medford site, and this is what it looks like.

110
00:05:54,518 --> 00:05:57,419
And it basically starts by asking you the question, what are you struggling with?

111
00:05:57,519 --> 00:05:59,180
So you could click on which one.

112
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:01,040
So we'll just say anxiety here.

113
00:06:01,580 --> 00:06:02,741
And then you go to the next step.

114
00:06:02,781 --> 00:06:04,461
It asks you for severity.

115
00:06:05,302 --> 00:06:06,442
We'll go for medium.

116
00:06:09,043 --> 00:06:10,983
Has the person seen the therapist before?

117
00:06:11,003 --> 00:06:11,043
No.

118
00:06:12,304 --> 00:06:13,184
Gender identity.

119
00:06:15,770 --> 00:06:17,151
Age, we'll just do adults.

120
00:06:18,951 --> 00:06:20,632
It asks you for your ethnicity.

121
00:06:22,612 --> 00:06:24,753
And then it asks you for insurance.

122
00:06:24,793 --> 00:06:25,893
I'm just going to press I don't know.

123
00:06:27,434 --> 00:06:35,616
And then it asks you for your zip code, how far you're willing to travel, and who it's for.

124
00:06:36,097 --> 00:06:39,798
So it's for myself or a staff member, right, student or staff member.

125
00:06:39,818 --> 00:06:40,678
I'll just press student.

126
00:06:41,898 --> 00:06:57,481
And what this does is it pulls up the both how you book an appointment so that you could call care cells directly and that they'll assist you, or you can go through and scan yourself.

127
00:06:57,961 --> 00:07:03,022
So you can say, oh, these are the providers near me that may be able to assist me.

128
00:07:03,143 --> 00:07:09,504
I'm gonna make these phone calls on my behalf, or I wanna start searching for who they are.

129
00:07:10,578 --> 00:07:17,744
The other option is either you call them directly and give them the same information, they'll start calling on your behalf to make appointments.

130
00:07:17,844 --> 00:07:23,870
So sometimes I'll get a call from a provider in our area and they say, are you working with this agency?

131
00:07:23,930 --> 00:07:31,376
Because they're calling saying they're trying to book an appointment for an adolescent who's at Medford High School.

132
00:07:31,456 --> 00:07:31,997
And I'll say, yes.

133
00:07:32,637 --> 00:07:43,522
They are assisting us but you need to talk with them as far as like insurance and payment work directly with the agency, who will then get consent from either the student if they're over 18 or their parent.

134
00:07:44,822 --> 00:07:49,784
And the goal here is that eventually over some back and forth and I'll show you.

135
00:07:51,085 --> 00:08:02,052
how many calls and emails they're making in a second, they will eventually call back and say, great, you know, we have an appointment for you in two weeks or two months or three months or whatever it is with this provider.

136
00:08:02,392 --> 00:08:03,573
Are you willing to accept it?

137
00:08:03,793 --> 00:08:05,594
And you can say yes or you can say no.

138
00:08:06,715 --> 00:08:14,399
And so we've had people decline services by saying, you know, no, it's too far or yes, that sounds great.

139
00:08:14,539 --> 00:08:14,819
And then

140
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:22,764
they'll respond back if it was a warm handoff through the school saying, we found this person a provider, they have an appointment in two months.

141
00:08:23,945 --> 00:08:29,928
CARESOLS also follows up with the person either after they have their appointment and they say, do you like this person?

142
00:08:29,948 --> 00:08:30,989
Did you like your appointment?

143
00:08:31,269 --> 00:08:33,670
And if they say yes, they consider that case closed.

144
00:08:34,311 --> 00:08:36,392
And if they say no, they start looking for somebody else.

145
00:08:38,804 --> 00:08:43,087
So again, you can either search on your own or go through the warm handoff process.

146
00:08:44,368 --> 00:08:45,208
So this is my.

147
00:08:46,943 --> 00:08:49,385
and you can see it says school staff login.

148
