202
00:13:41,386 --> 00:13:43,327
People are clicking on more than one area here.

203
00:13:44,467 --> 00:13:51,408
So 8% marital disruptive, trauma, 27% depression and anxiety.

204
00:13:52,048 --> 00:13:53,608
That's the breakdown that I expected here.

205
00:13:53,628 --> 00:13:57,509
I'm gonna stop sharing my screen and I'll answer.

206
00:13:58,964 --> 00:14:00,165
Any questions you all have?

207
00:14:00,185 --> 00:14:14,293
Stacey, I guess I'm curious about folks who don't have any insurance.

208
00:14:15,014 --> 00:14:21,998
It's sort of the program sort of reducing the friction between someone who thinks they might need help and an avenue to get it.

209
00:14:22,559 --> 00:14:26,261
But I'm also thinking about families that don't have the insurance to get the help.

210
00:14:26,852 --> 00:14:27,252
That's right.

211
00:14:27,452 --> 00:14:31,594
So, ideally, we would cross that bridge before we're making that referral.

212
00:14:32,194 --> 00:14:41,538
And for someone to say I don't have insurance, and then problem solve around that at the school level, either by assisting them with accessing insurance or mass health.

213
00:14:42,584 --> 00:14:52,592
or problem solving in another way, or if they're searching on their own and they allow us to be a partner with them, they would say, we don't have insurance.

214
00:14:53,072 --> 00:15:00,538
And then they would come back to us and say, hey, your warm handoff responded back to us stating that they're not accessing care because they don't have insurance.

215
00:15:00,838 --> 00:15:02,399
And then we work with the family around that.

216
00:15:02,579 --> 00:15:03,360
But that's a great question.

217
00:15:04,872 --> 00:15:10,395
I mean, the back and forth communication with Care Solace, like we are, it is a real in time moment.

218
00:15:11,315 --> 00:15:17,518
So Neil, if you were, if I was referring you, your name is on my screen and it tells me every time they're contacting you.

219
00:15:17,959 --> 00:15:22,361
And then they have a blurb out to me to say, oh, by the way, there's an insurance challenge here.

220
00:15:22,381 --> 00:15:23,241
Can you help us with this?

221
00:15:23,341 --> 00:15:24,802
And then we problem solve from there.

222
00:15:26,143 --> 00:15:34,107
But this is solving the gap of both parents and students not knowing how to navigate the system or even who to contact for it.

223
00:15:34,587 --> 00:15:38,590
And counselors, frankly, just don't have the time to make 15 phone calls a day for one family.

224
00:15:39,270 --> 00:15:53,280
So we're sending resources to them over and over again, but we don't have the time to make those individual phone calls when they're not always connected, unless it's to a big partner for a specific service that we are saying, oh, this is the niche that you fall into.

225
00:15:53,340 --> 00:15:54,141
We know exactly.

226
00:15:55,112 --> 00:15:56,353
who to refer you to here.

227
00:15:57,714 --> 00:16:00,216
But again, there are only so many appointments.

228
00:16:01,336 --> 00:16:04,158
And so many appointments that fit into people's schedules, too.

229
00:16:04,619 --> 00:16:06,940
